<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Determining the size (order) of given matrices</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Give the size (order) of each of the following matrices as \((\text{number of rows}) \times (\text{number of columns})\). Enter whole numbers only.</p>
<ol style="list-style-type: lower-alpha;">
  <li>
    <p>\({@mat1@} \quad \text{size} = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] \(\times\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]]</p>
    <p>[[feedback:prt1]]</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p>\({@mat2@} \quad \text{size} = \) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] \(\times\) [[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]]</p>
    <p>[[feedback:prt2]]</p>
  </li>
</ol>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>
<p>The <strong>size (order)</strong> of a matrix is written as \((\text{number of rows}) \times (\text{number of columns})\).</p>
<ol style="list-style-type: lower-alpha;">
  <li>
    <p>The matrix
    \[{@mat1@}\]
    has \({@m1@}\) rows and \({@n1@}\) columns. Therefore, its size is \(\boxed{{@m1@} \times {@n1@}}\).</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p>The matrix
    \[{@mat2@}\]
    has \({@m2@}\) rows and \({@n2@}\) columns. Therefore, its size is \(\boxed{{@m2@} \times {@n2@}}\).</p>
  </li>
</ol>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
